    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Tipping is an important part of American culture. People usually leave a tip for service workers like "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or taxi drivers. But nowadays, they not only need to give extra money to human workers—even "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "self-checkout machines",
            "zh": "自助结账机"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are asking for tips too. This new situation has made many Americans feel "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and confused."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Self-checkout machines are now "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in stores across big cities. However, most people don’t like the idea of leaving a tip at these machines at all. With these machines, there’s no face-to-face communication or "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " service between people. Customers do all the work themselves by scanning and bagging items. The use of self-checkout machines has already reduced "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "labour costs",
            "zh": "人力成本"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for businesses. “Then who am I tipping? Where’s the money going? I’m doing all the work myself!” asked one angry customer. Many people feel this isn’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The businesses seem to have their own "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for setting up these tip requests. “All tips collected go to our employees,” explained one company "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "representative",
            "ref": "v-representative"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “And remember, tipping is completely "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "optional",
            "ref": "v-optional"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and up to each customer.” "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", it’s the customers’ own decision whether to leave a tip and how much to give. Still, many people feel uncomfortable when the machine asks for "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " money. The screen shows different tip amounts and they have to make a "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". What would you do if you were in America facing this situation? Would you press the tip button or "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
